# PageFlip mismatch test, RIGHT half (slot 1). This instance is started with a different screen
# margin, so its viewport -- and therefore its layout hash -- cannot match the left half's
# (docs/pageflip.md section 5). It must notice, say so, and refuse to pair.
#
# Receives no input at all after opening the book. The left instance presses throughout, and the
# point of the test is that none of those presses move this device: an incompatible peer that still
# gated the two-step advance would leave the pair silently desynced.
log pageflip-mismatch-right: start
expect_timeout 60000
expect Entering activity: Home
wait 800
tap confirm
expect Entering activity: EpubReader
wait 9000
# Detection happens on the greeting, before any turn has been applied.
expect incompatible layout
screenshot /screenshots/pf-mm-right-00.bmp
# Long enough for both of the left half's presses to arrive and be rejected.
wait 14000
screenshot /screenshots/pf-mm-right-01.bmp
log pageflip-mismatch-right: done
quit
